     "pull_request": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/qdrant/qdrant/pulls/9442",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/qdrant/qdrant/pull/9442",
      "diff_url": "https://github.com/qdrant/qdrant/pull/9442.diff",
      "patch_url": "https://github.com/qdrant/qdrant/pull/9442.patch",
      "merged_at": null
     },
     "body": "`POST /cluster/recover` (and the cluster metadata update path) constructed `StorageError::ServiceError` when no consensus is configured, mapping to HTTP 500 / gRPC `Internal`. Standalone mode is an expected configuration, not a server fault, so this changes both sites to `BadRequest` → HTTP 400 / gRPC `InvalidArgument`, matching the existing behavior of `DELETE /cluster/peer/{id}` (\"Distributed mode disabled.\").\n\nOnly two call sites use `get_consensus_proposal_sender()`, both user-facing; the internal raft snapshot path in `consensus.rs` is unrelated.\n\nFixes #9421\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
     "reactions": {
